7. **`upper_lower_d5_odd`** (Erdős–Pach): the refined $n^{4/3}$ error term for odd $d \ge 5$.

These are major theorems whose complete proofs span many pages of research literature (the Szemerédi–Trotter theorem alone is a substantial argument involving the crossing lemma and careful graph decomposition; the Lenz construction and Erdős–Pach refinements require intricate geometric and graph-theoretic machinery). Furthermore, variant `upper_d3` is explicitly an **open problem** — no proof is known.

